=== Test 3: multi-column CASE condition with > (col-vs-col) ===
== Query ==
SELECT c.c_id,
SUM(CASE WHEN c.c_region > c.c_floor THEN c.c_region ELSE 0 END) AS s
FROM cte_customer AS c
JOIN cte_orders AS o ON o.o_custkey = c.c_id
GROUP BY c.c_id;

Number of output lines, including header: 4

== Diff ==
==========



== Expected result ==
SELECT c.c_id,
SUM(CASE WHEN c.c_region > c.c_floor THEN c.c_region ELSE 0 END) AS s
FROM cte_customer AS c
JOIN cte_orders AS o ON o.o_custkey = c.c_id
GROUP BY c.c_id|
c_id	s
100	0
200	0
300	0


